---
import ContentLayout from "@/layouts/ContentLayout.astro";
import { siteConfig } from "@/config/site";
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Terms of Use | Dubai Battery Service"
  description="Terms of use for dubaibatteryservice.com — how the information and service-request links on this website work."
  path="/terms/"
  crumbs={[
    { name: "Home", path: "/" },
    { name: "Terms of use", path: "/terms/" },
  ]}
  eyebrow="Legal"
  h1="Terms of Use"
  lead="The basics of how this website and its service-request links work."
  heroCtas={false}
  sidebar={false}
  ctaBand={false}
>
  <p><em>Last updated: 24 September 2026</em></p>

  <h2>About this website</h2>
  <p>
    {siteConfig.siteName} provides information about car batteries in Dubai and a way to request mobile battery help.
    Service requests made through the WhatsApp and call buttons are fulfilled by an independent mobile battery team, which
    supplies the batteries, carries out the work and provides the warranty. Your service agreement — including price,
    warranty and payment — is with that team.
  </p>

  <h2>Prices and information</h2>
  <p>
    Prices shown on this site are indicative ranges, not quotes. Your actual price depends on your car and the battery you
    choose, and is confirmed before any work begins. Technical information is general guidance — always follow your
    vehicle manufacturer's specification.
  </p>

  <h2>Response times</h2>
  <p>
    Stated arrival times are typical, not guaranteed. Traffic, weather, access and demand can all affect how quickly a
    technician reaches you.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    We take care to keep the information on this site accurate, but it is provided "as is". To the extent permitted by UAE
    law, we are not liable for decisions made on the basis of the website content alone.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions about these terms? Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
</ContentLayout>
